7. Design round 4: source of the rendered pixel measurements cited here

$ bash -lc cd /Users/damian/workspace/mobile-i18n-d5aaf8ba6ba5/mobile-i18n && gh pr view 132 --json comments --jq '.comments[].body' | grep -n 'Ended composer field content box\|requires \*\*276.9\|Envoyer rouvre…\|Rouvre la session…\|Envoyez pour rouvrir…\|Rouvre dans votre dossier…' | head -20
750:- Ended composer field content box: **348 px** at 390 pt, **278 px** at 320 pt.
751:- `Rouvre dans votre dossier personnel…` (36 cells) requires **276.9 px at 100 %**, **354.4 px at the app's 135 % step**, **388.7 px at 150 %**, **590.9 px at 200 %**.
767:| `Envoyer rouvre…` | 15 | 120.7 | 256.8 | yes (21 px spare) |
768:| `Rouvre la session…` | 18 | 138.7 | 295.9 | no |
769:| `Envoyez pour rouvrir…` | 21 | 160.6 | 342.9 | no |
770:| `Rouvre dans votre dossier…` | 27 | 200.8 | 429.4 | no |
776:`Send to reopen in your home folder…` tells the reader that sending is what reopens; `Rouvre dans votre dossier personnel…` says only that the session reopens, leaving the subject implicit. The register itself is right, and I want to be explicit because this is the point I doubted before measuring: `Rouvre` is the same third-person form the app already uses on its own hints (`Ouvre le menu de la session`, `Ouvre la ligne d'activité, les tâches et les sous-agents`), and the French runs 20 `vous` forms against 3 of those constructions across the 143 strings — there is no tu/vous break inside the string. The residual risk is that a bare verb in an empty message box also reads as an instruction to the reader, pointing at an action the field does not offer. D1's remedy closes it for free: `Envoyer rouvre…` restores the action English carries and is the shortest measured fit.
[exit=0]

